WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.567
Donald Trump is

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:02.702
under multiple criminal inquiries,

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:03.436
but there are signs

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.005
he may face charges

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.539
in the first of those this week.

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:06.840
For more,

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.807
I want to talk to the reporter

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:08.842
who perhaps knows

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:09.576
Trump, the best

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:10.677
senior political correspondent

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.978
for The New York Times, Maggie Haberman,

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.747
who has been awarded a Pulitzer Prize

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:14.781
for her coverage of the former

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.082
president Maggie.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:16.950
Behind the scenes,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.884
what can you tell us about

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:20.453
how Trump is handling this situation?

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:21.721
Look, Jake,

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.622
he's very anxious

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.858
about the prospect of being indicted

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.092
for a couple of reasons.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.261
Yes. Two things can be true at once.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.129
He is aware

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.897
that there are reasons to believe

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.132
this could help him politically.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.333
We have heard a lot about this

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.567
this morning already,

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.302
but he does not want to face

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:36.936
getting arrested,

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:37.804
which is what happens

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:38.772
when you get indicted.

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:40.774
You get fingerprinted you get brought in.

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.175
You have to ask for bail.

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:43.109
None of that is something

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.310
that he is excited about.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.779
So he and his folks,

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.414
his his political folks

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:48.181
are preparing

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.083
for a huge blitz politically

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.317
to push back on the Manhattan

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.052
district attorney.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.553
You saw that start yesterday,

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.921
although I don't think that his true

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:55.922
social post yesterday

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:58.558
morning calling for protests was part of

00:00:58.558 --> 00:00:59.793
part of a grand plan.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:00.260
He did it

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:00.994
and a bunch of his aides

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:02.162
were surprised by it.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.630
But I do think that that is separate

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.831
from what you're going to see

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:05.932
legally and.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:06.299
Well,

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.901
I know that his folks are suggesting

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.235
this is a weak case.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.103
They don't actually know

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.137
what the evidence is.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.039
What it is is trivial compared

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.307
to the other inquiries.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:14.941
That doesn't mean

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.176
there won't be a conviction

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:18.111
and they have to be mindful of that.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.312
Trump called in his supporters,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.013
as you noted,

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.114
to protest and, quote,

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:22.849
take our nation back

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.150
on that truth social post.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.919
Obviously, the last time

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:26.753
Donald Trump

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.488
called for his supporters to rally,

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:30.390
it resulted in an insurrection

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.558
at the Capitol.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.960
Does he have any concern about violence?

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:34.694
No.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.196
This is not something that,

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:36.729
you know,

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.131
he expresses enormous concern

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.132
about to anyone.

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:39.632
That doesn't

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.001
mean people around him are not concerned

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:44.204
about what he's saying about protest.

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:46.673
And they are because as you know well,

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.541
he is still under investigation.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:49.442
One of these inquiries

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.643
by the Justice Department

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:51.778
is about the events

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.813
leading up to January 6th and his efforts

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.081
to stay in power.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:55.915
And there have been

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.317
lots of people, hundreds

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.751
arrested in connection

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.320
with that attack on the Capitol.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.388
So this is not something he voices

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:03.590
a whole lot of concern about,

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.525
but it is absolutely something folks in

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:06.326
his world

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:07.560
are mindful of that

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.129
this is going to keep coming up,

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.131
especially as he pushes this.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.233
And this is having an effect

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.935
of rallying Republicans around him.

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.403
I mean, you have Speaker McCarthy

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.172
calling it an outrageous abuse of power.

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.740
That that's not that surprising.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:21.708
He's he's

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:22.742
always been very supportive

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:23.443
of Donald Trump,

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.145
but even would be rival

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:26.913
Mike Pence says he's taken aback

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:27.280
and he says

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.948
it reeks of political prosecution.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.084
We heard Governor Sununu today

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:33.353
suggesting that he didn't think this was.

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:33.820
This rose

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:34.888
to the magnitude

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:37.157
of of such an unprecedented action.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.559
We still have not heard, however,

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:41.895
from Nikki Haley or from Ron DeSantis.

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:42.262
What do you think

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:44.030
is the political calculus there?

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.598
I think that Ron DeSantis is going to try

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.033
to avoid weighing in on this

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.434
as long as possible,

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:48.935
and he will

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:49.536
then decide

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:51.437
whether as long as possible has been met.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.339
You saw yesterday on Twitter

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.241
one of Trump's advisers, Jason Miller,

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.443
highlighting that DeSantis has not said

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:57.977
anything yet.

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:59.245
DeSantis is obviously

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.313
the governor of the state

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:01.147
where Trump lives.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:02.849
And, you know, should Trump decide

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.317
he's not going to surrender?

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:06.686
Should that not happen? Peacefully?

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:07.453
If he is indicted

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.422
and expected to be charged,

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:10.089
then DeSantis

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:11.357
would have to make some decisions.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:12.926
And so this gets very complicated.

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:13.526
Trump's own

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.427
folks are aware

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:15.862
and this came up last week

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.730
repeatedly as I was reporting this out.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.798
They believed that

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.333
if Trump was to be charged,

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.402
this could put his rivals in a bind,

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:23.970
especially Ron DeSantis,

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.072
because they are going to be called upon

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.140
to speak out against it.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.107
And as you just noted,

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:29.943
the pressure is already building.

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.010
So Trump says he's committed

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.478
to staying in the 20, 24 race,

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:35.215
even if he is indicted

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:36.749
That sounds

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.084
completely characteristic,

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:40.119
but is it realistic?

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:41.888
I don't think it's unrealistic,

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.723
depending on what else happens, Jake.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.458
If it is just this case,

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:45.959
then I think

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.760
it isn't unrealistic that he stays in,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.962
although we have no idea

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.763
exactly when a trial would be.

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.031
Would it even be this year?

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.733
Would it stretch into next year?

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.267
The point

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.802
I think, is that we are talking about

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.570
potentially multiple indictments.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.905
We are talking about an indictment

00:03:58.905 --> 00:03:59.539
in Georgia

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.274
possibly happening in the coming months.

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:02.041
We are talking about

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.009
indictment, indictments

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:04.110
from the federal government

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.345
happening in the coming months.

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:08.381
That becomes a lot of freight to carry

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.716
in a presidential race.

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:11.784
And you can start to see a world

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:13.319
where Republicans might say

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.188
on this one case in Manhattan,

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:17.257
we feel it's you know, it's trivial.

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.424
But these other cases,

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.460
this drip, drip, it's just constant drama

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.028
and let's move on. We'll see.

